In article <2a8a3414wnr070@ark.abg.sub.org> ralf@ark.abg.sub.org (Ralf Stephan) writes:
>I would like to draw your attention to a possible violation of the GNU
>license. There is a German shareware game named GOR which is probably
>derived from Nethack code. Especially the game commands and messages are
>direct translations from Nethack ones, as well as the object types and
>behaviours and the character stats, though the 3D look and the generated
>levels are somewhat different and there is only one character type.
>
>Could the Dev Team or someone from GNU comment on a case like this?  I'm
>willing to mail a sample of the demo version if I'm asked to, but only one
>or two, since I have to pay for every K of mail.

   I've forwarded your message to the Nethack maintainers.  The copyright
is theirs, not the FSF's, although they use the GPL on their software.
They said they would look into it. 

   I should mention that this is only a concern if actual source code has
been copied, not if the game merely appears similar in appearance to the
end user. 



